+# Proposals awaiting Justin, from the entropy assessment of 2026-10-07
+
+**Status: proposed. Neither is a decision.** Work that depends on either waits for Justin's recorded answer, which
+goes in this folder as its own dated file naming this one.
+
+## P1. What ORC may reach, and whether its lists are rules or descriptions
+
+ORC's `AGENTS.md` ("Boundaries") says subprocess access exists in three named modules and direct network access only
+in `src/core/research-tools.ts` and `src/adapters/notifications/ntfy.ts`, and that no model or agent reaches the ntfy
+transport. The code, read on 2026-10-07, also has:
+
+- `src/adapters/orc-service.ts`: git reads, a frozen-lockfile pnpm install and `systemctl --user restart orc.service`
+  (orchestrator#101). `test/architecture.test.ts` already approves it; `AGENTS.md` does not list it.
+- `src/adapters/browser/playwright.ts`: one headless Chromium per approved browser session, which reaches the
+  approved hosts, receives the approved login (storage state), and makes DNS lookups (orchestrator#76, #197).
+  Neither `AGENTS.md` nor `test/architecture.test.ts` lists it, and the test's patterns do not detect it.
+- `src/adapters/phone/index.ts`: a package that declares the built-in `phone` connector sends its agent's notice
+  (title, text, tap address, tags) through ORC's ntfy sender (orchestrator#184).
+
+Proposed: Justin confirms each of the three reaches, or says which is not authorised; the Boundaries lists become the
+rule that `test/architecture.test.ts` enforces, so a new reach fails a test until it is recorded; and `AGENTS.md`
+and `README.md` are then corrected to match the confirmed lists. The draft corrections are the assessment's
+provisional patch.
+
+## P2. Rises in the core-tie allowance of `config/installation.ts`
+
+`AGENTS.md` says a core-tie count "may only fall, and its allowance falls in the same change". The Scope allowance
+for `config/installation.ts` in `test/core-ties.ts` rose 28 → 51 → 64 → 70 between 28 Sep and 2 Oct, each rise
+explained in a comment and none citing a decision of Justin's. The test checks only that each count equals its
+allowance, so nothing stops a rise.
+
+Proposed: Justin records whether rises in `config/installation.ts` are allowed until Scopes load by card
+(orchestrator#152), each citing that decision, with every other rise refused; or whether each rise needs its own
+recorded decision.
